    abstract = {This article explores the growing importance of cybersecurity for digital museum mobile applications. The ever-increasing reliance on digital technologies necessitates robust security measures to protect sensitive information and user privacy. The work discusses the benefits of digital museums, including their ability to reach a global audience and provide engaging, enriching experiences. It then highlights key cybersecurity challenges faced by digital museums, such as data breaches and malware attacks. The conclusion emphasizes the need for a multi-layered approach to cybersecurity, encompassing secure development practices, user education, and adherence to data privacy regulations.},
