    abstract = {Academic library and information science (LIS) faculty members educate those who will work in libraries and other types of information-related organizations (e.g. museums, schools, etc.), including library workers, librarians, and information professionals. They usually perform a mix of teaching, service, and research activities. A minimum credential required for LIS faculty is typically a master׳s degree, but often a doctorate or PhD is required. The work of academic LIS faculty is continuously evolving, requiring LIS faculty to keep up with the rapidly changing field of library and information science, accreditation and other standards, and societal needs and trends.},
