    abstract = {Social media refers to web-based mass communication tools that enable users to network and share ideas, information, and messages. Tech companies constantly introduce new social media platforms to meet the increasing needs of the global population. Each year, the number of social media users rises. This entry aims to introduce social media, describe how its usage has increased in the Library and Information Science (LIS) field, and provide examples of how LIS professionals use social media. The discussion explores the influence of social media on the LIS field, including a bibliometric summary that illustrates the growth of social media discourse in LIS literature.},
